:::oak-heading {id="task-b" level="2"}
Task B: Why the Nile mattered
:::
:::oak-instruction {id="reading" keep-with-next="true"}
The Ancient Egyptians lived beside a long, deep river they called the Nile, in North Africa. Dry land on either side protected them from their enemies.
:::
:::oak-question {id="question-2" number="2" marks="2"}
The Nile carried a dark black mud. Explain what happened to the land when the river flooded.
